  <string name="perm_denied_title">What to do if it is denied</string>
  <string name="perm_safe_text">Why it is safe: the internet is used only to check and download updates. Notifications are not sent anywhere. The source code is open for review.</string>
  <string name="perm_overlay_why">The island is drawn over other apps. The app does not read what you do on the screen.</string>
  <string name="perm_overlay_steps">How to enable: 1) tap “Open settings”; 2) find Live Island in the list; 3) turn the switch on; 4) return to the app.</string>
  <string name="perm_denied_overlay">If the switch does not respond, close other windows and try again. On some phones you first need to allow restricted settings, as for notifications (see the step above).</string>
  <string name="perm_listener_why">The app reads notifications only to show them in the island. Nothing is saved or sent.</string>
  <string name="perm_listener_steps">How to enable: 1) tap “Open settings”; 2) find Live Island in the list; 3) enable access and confirm; 4) return to the app.</string>
  <string name="perm_denied_listener">Android 13 and newer may block notification access for apps not installed from a store. What to do: 1) open Settings → Apps → Live Island; 2) tap the three dots at the top right; 3) choose “Allow restricted settings”; 4) return and enable notification access.</string>
  <string name="perm_install_title">Installing the update</string>
  <string name="perm_install_why">Needed only to install the downloaded update. Without it the app still works, but cannot be updated from inside.</string>
  <string name="perm_install_steps">How to enable: 1) tap “Open settings”; 2) turn on “Allow from this source”; 3) return and tap “Download” again.</string>
  <string name="perm_denied_install">If the option is unavailable, open Settings → Apps → Live Island → “Install unknown apps” and turn it on.</string>
  <string name="perm_battery_title">Background work</string>
  <string name="perm_battery_why">So the system does not turn the island off in the background.</string>
  <string name="perm_battery_steps">How to enable: 1) tap “Open settings”; 2) choose Live Island; 3) select “Don’t optimize” or “Unrestricted”.</string>
  <string name="perm_denied_battery">If there is no such option, open Settings → Apps → Live Island → Battery and choose “Unrestricted”. On Xiaomi, Huawei and Samsung also enable autostart for Live Island.</string>
  <string name="onb1_t">Hi! This is Live Island</string>
  <string name="onb1_b">A dynamic island for Android: it shows what matters at the top edge of the screen and hides when there is nothing to show.</string>
  <string name="onb2_t">Everything important at a glance</string>
  <string name="onb2_b">Calls, music and messages from any app, plus charging status. Each event has its own color that adapts to your wallpaper.</string>
  <string name="onb3_t">Tap and hold</string>
  <string name="onb3_b">A short tap expands the island, a long press hides it. When expanded there are buttons: answer a call, open a message.</string>
  <string name="onb4_t">It hides when not needed</string>
  <string name="onb4_b">If nothing is happening, the island disappears completely. Music playing? It stays compact, a new message appears on top and then music returns.</string>
  <string name="onb5_t">Display over other apps</string>
  <string name="onb5_b">Needed so the island can be drawn above any app and game. Why it is safe: the app only draws the island and reads notifications to show them there. Nothing is sent anywhere.</string>
  <string name="onb6_t">Notification access</string>
  <string name="onb6_b">So the island can see calls, music and messages from all apps: Telegram, WhatsApp, YouTube Music and any others. Why it is safe: the app only draws the island and reads notifications to show them there. Nothing is sent anywhere.</string>
  <string name="onb7_t">Background work</string>
  <string name="onb7_b">So the system does not turn the island off, allow unrestricted work. On Xiaomi, Huawei, Samsung and OPPO also enable autostart for Live Island. Why it is safe: the app only draws the island and reads notifications to show them there. Nothing is sent anywhere.</string>
  <string name="onb8_t">Set it up your way</string>
  <string name="onb8_b">In the “Look” tab choose the theme, island color and animation speed. In “Island settings” set position, offset, size and what to show.</string>
  <string name="onb9_t">All set</string>
  <string name="onb9_b">The island will start and show a tip. You can reopen the tutorial any time from the home screen.</string>
